   "CHARACTER SHEET - HareHeat   (bake FIRST, before any scene)\n\nSame make as the book: a flat fill with a broad reed-pen contour drawn in the OTHER fill colour,\ndry skipping line. Draw this sheet on a SPLIT GROUND - the left half sun ochre #C9903C, the right\nhalf shade blue-green #2C4038 - so both states of the animal are settled at once. No white\nanywhere on this sheet, and no bare paper.\n\nFACE: young hare, long head, small round muzzle. A drawn eye with a SEPARATE pen brow above it -\n  the brows do the acting and must lift, pull together and tilt unevenly. Whiskers 3 strokes a\n  side. The tongue, when it hangs out panting, is CONTOUR ONLY with no colour inside it.\nEARS: 🔴 THE GAUGE, and the only place the accent red is ever used. Two tall ears; when they fold\n  flat sideways the inside faces the reader. Draw the ladder as three heads in a row, same size\n  and same angle, differing only in the flat step inside the ear: pale #E6B7A6 / flushed #D0664A /\n  scarlet #B22B18. A child must be able to name which is hottest with the sheet across a room.\nBODY: long and loose, four heads tall standing, low and stretched when it lies down. Long hind\n  legs, small forepaws, short lifted tail.\n🔴 IN SUN / IN SHADE (draw the same pose twice, once on each half of the split ground): in sun the\n  body is an ochre shape with a blue-green outline and AT MOST 3 marks inside it; in shade it is a\n  blue-green shape with ochre hatching along the flank and haunch. Same drawing, opposite make.\nSHEET: on hind legs with one forepaw thrown up / four legs braced skidding to a stop, forepaws\n  ploughing forward / lying flat on the belly with all four legs stretched out and the ears spread\n  wide sideways / one forepaw pulling its own ear down so the inside faces us / leaping with all\n  four feet off the ground; plus two close-ups - eyes screwed shut with the mouth wide open\n  panting, and eyes wide open having just understood something. Plain split ground, no road.\nSCENE token: HareHeat.",
