   "CHARACTER SHEET - HillSet   (bake THIRD - the stage, used on every page)\n\nThe road, empty of animals, exactly as it sits on all fourteen pages. Two flat fills, reed-pen\nline in the other colour, and no bare paper anywhere.\n\nTHE PLACE: one ochre dirt road climbing from the bottom of the frame to a big tree at the top of\n  the hill, curving as it goes. Dry grass either side as at most 20 short strokes. Cypresses stand\n  apart along the road, each ONE flat blue-green shape with at most 7 notches on its edge, 0\n  needles, 0 trunk lines. A low stone wall and rolling ridges far off as at most 3 wavering lines.\n🔴 THE EDGE IS THE SUBJECT OF THIS SHEET - draw the road four times in a row, same viewpoint,\n  changing only where the sun/shade edge falls:\n  A · EARLY MORNING - long blue-green bands lying right across the ochre road, three of them.\n  B · LATE MORNING - one clean diagonal edge cutting the frame, wide shade on one side.\n  C · NOON - the shade shrunk to the width of a cypress trunk at its foot; the rest all ochre.\n  D · EVENING - wide bands again, alternating, neither colour winning.\n  Every edge is cut clean. 🔴 Put A and C side by side and check that the shade is a SHAPE WITH\n  AN AREA, not a darker mood.\n🔴 SUN HAS NO LINES IN IT: on the ochre, things get a contour and at most 3 marks. On the\n  blue-green, the same things carry ochre hatching. Show one cypress standing half in each so the\n  difference is settled.\nALSO ON THIS SHEET: a hare-belly hollow pressed into the shade earth · a short line of hare prints\n  on the ochre · one cicada on a branch as 4 marks · a single ochre disc for the low evening sun,\n  sitting inside a blue-green ground. 0 lettering, 0 numerals, 0 signs.\nSCENE token: HillSet."
